course: dictionary
lesson: 3473
title: A fast bird of prey
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A falcon is a bird of prey, which means a bird that hunts other animals for food. Read the words around a new word to find its meaning. «At the bird of prey show, a falcon drops onto a swinging lure» tells you the falcon swoops down fast onto something.
explain: «The peregrine falcon is the fastest animal, diving at over three hundred kilometres an hour with its wings folded like a bullet.» Fastest and bullet are clues that the falcon moves very quickly. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: a fast bird of prey fits.
explain: Some animals look alike but are not close relatives. «Falcons look like hawks, but DNA, the tiny instructions inside every living cell, shows they are closer cousins of parrots and songbirds.» The word but tells you the sentence is about to show a difference from how they look.
fact: A falcon is a fast bird of prey with long pointed wings and a hooked beak.
fact: Falcons catch other birds and small animals.
fact: The peregrine falcon is the fastest animal on Earth when it dives through the air.
fact: Falcons look like hawks, but DNA shows they are closer cousins of parrots and songbirds.
fact: Peregrine falcons nest on tall buildings and hunt city pigeons.
exercise: What is a falcon? | *A fast bird of prey with long pointed wings | A tall building in a city | A kind of tree that grows on cliffs | A fish that swims in deep rivers
exercise: «The peregrine falcon is the fastest animal on Earth when it dives through the air.» What does fastest mean here? | *Moves quicker than any other animal | Has the loudest call | Flies in the highest places | Sits still for the longest time
exercise: Find and copy one word from «a falcon drops onto a swinging lure» that tells you the falcon moves downwards. | swinging | lure | *drops | falcon
test: «Falcons look like hawks, but DNA shows they are closer cousins of parrots and songbirds.» What does the word but tell you? | *The sentence is about to show a difference from how they look | It ends the sentence | It means the hawk is a parrot | It means the falcon is slow
test: Which word means an animal that is hunted and eaten by another animal? | *prey | cathedral | nest | pigeon
exam: «A diving peregrine can go faster than 300 kilometres per hour.» What do the words faster than tell you about the falcon? | It is very quiet | It sits on a tall building | *It moves very quickly | It is a pigeon
